.TH EGGHEAD-SERVE 1 "April 2026" "egghead 0.1.0" "Egghead Manual"
.SH NAME
egghead-serve \- web and MCP HTTP server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B egghead serve
.RB [ \-\-port
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-i | \-\-interactive ]
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR PATH ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Start the web server and MCP HTTP endpoint. The MCP endpoint is
available at
.B /mcp
on the same port. Logs go to stdout.
.PP
For the MCP stdio transport (editor integration), use
.BR egghead-mcp (1)
instead.
.SH FLAGS
.TP
.B \-\-port \fIN\fR
Override the HTTP port. Default: 4000.
.TP
.B \-i, \-\-interactive
Keep the BEAM break menu available (Ctrl+C to inspect). Without this
flag, Ctrl+C exits cleanly.
.TP
.B \-\-config \fIPATH\fR
Override config file location.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help text.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
egghead serve
egghead serve \-\-port 8080
egghead serve \-\-interactive
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR egghead-mcp (1),
.BR egghead-config (1),
.BR egghead-doctor (1),
.BR egghead (1)
